From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Andrei-Alexandru Bleortu <me@andrei-z.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 19:23:01 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: ath11k: no regulatory failure for the rules a recovery
 repeats

After a firmware restart the firmware sends its default regulatory rules
again. ath11k_reg_handle_chan_list() deliberately keeps the pdev's
existing default regd then, but returned -EINVAL for that, so every
recovery logged "failed to process regulatory info -22". For the
event's own rules (power type unset), free them and return 0, like the
rules that would overwrite an identical default regd; a power type
update passes the stored rules, which are not ours to free, and keeps
its result.

Assisted-by: LLM
---
 drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/reg.c | 10 ++++++++++
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/reg.c b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/reg.c
index 2ac9156..c9a48af 100644
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/reg.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/reg.c
@@ -755,6 +755,16 @@ int ath11k_reg_handle_chan_list(struct ath11k_base *ab,
 	if (test_bit(ATH11K_FLAG_RECOVERY, &ab->dev_flags) &&
 	    ab->default_regd[pdev_idx]) {
 		spin_unlock_bh(&ab->base_lock);
+		/* The firmware's event repeats the rules the pdev has, and
+		 * the event's reg_info is ours to free; the stored one of a
+		 * power type update is not.
+		 */
+		if (power_type == IEEE80211_REG_UNSET_AP) {
+			ath11k_dbg(ab, ATH11K_DBG_WMI,
+				   "recovery: default regulatory rules unchanged\n");
+			ath11k_reg_reset_info(reg_info);
+			return 0;
+		}
 		goto retfail;
 	}
 	spin_unlock_bh(&ab->base_lock);
